       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg, and this patient has no renal or hepatic impairment or other factor that would explain it. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged vasodilation, because amlodipine has a long half-life.\n\nCould this be a typo? Here are some options:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose. It can be titrated up to 10 mg.\n- **A different regimen**, such as adding a second agent if the goal is more blood pressure control.\n\nIf you do want 30 mg daily, please confirm that explicitly and tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?"
      }
